Load: SDD

Purpose:
  Load testing — verify system behavior under expected and peak load.
  Load tests simulate real user traffic to identify breaking points,
  resource exhaustion, and degradation patterns.

Owns: ./

Scope:
  Expected load (normal traffic)
  Peak load (traffic spikes)
  Stress testing (breaking point)
  Endurance testing (sustained load)
  Spike testing (sudden traffic increases)

Principles:
  Test with realistic traffic patterns
  Test with production-like data volume
  Monitor all system resources
  Identify bottlenecks before they cause outages
  Load tests are not just "make it fast" — they verify stability

Structure:
  Every load test MUST:
    define load profile (users, duration, ramp-up)
    define success criteria
    monitor system resources
    produce actionable results

Frameworks:
  k6
  Gatling
  JMeter
  Locust
  Artillery

LoadProfiles:
  Expected:
    users: expected concurrent users
    duration: 10-30 minutes
    ramp-up: gradual

  Peak:
    users: 2-3x expected
    duration: 5-15 minutes
    ramp-up: moderate

  Stress:
    users: increasing until failure
    duration: until system breaks
    ramp-up: gradual increase

  Endurance:
    users: expected load
    duration: 4-24 hours
    ramp-up: immediate

Navigation:
  Project: @project/project.sdd
  Workflow: @workflow/testing.sdd
  TestLevels: @levels.sdd
  TestTypes: @types.sdd
  TestGates: @gates.sdd
